(footprint "USB_C_Receptacle_HRO_TYPE-C-31-M-04"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "USB Type-C receptacle, 24-pin full-featured (both SuperSpeed pair rows + CC/D+-/SBU), authored Task 14 to replace the incomplete stock KiCad Connector_USB:USB_C_Receptacle_HRO_TYPE-C-31-M-17.kicad_mod, which only exposes 6 of the 24 required signal pads (A5/A9/A12/B5/B9/B12, i.e. just CC1/CC2/VBUS/GND) plus 4 mechanical shield legs -- confirmed against HRO's own manufacturer datasheet (LCSC C283540, datasheet.lcsc.com/datasheet/pdf/26d9c5bff410f020782d77a1fd4062b2.pdf) that TYPE-C-31-M-17 is in fact a 6-pin CC/VBUS/GND-only 'DETECTOR SWITCHS' receptacle, NOT a 24-pin SuperSpeed part -- the MPN pinned for J1 in docs/sourcing.md Task 7 does not physically match the 24-signal schematic symbol sierra-to-usb:USB_C_Receptacle_USB3.2_24P. Pin numbering/names in THIS footprint are taken from the real HRO TYPE-C-31-M-04 datasheet (LCSC C129018, the genuine 24-pin 'USB3.1(TYPE/C) female receptacle' in the same HRO TYPE-C-31 family), whose pin table matches the project J1 symbol pin-for-pin, name-for-name. Pad X pitch (0.50mm) and pad width (0.30mm) are taken directly from the M-04 datasheet's recommended-PCB-layout dimensions; row separation, pad length, and shield-leg placement are APPROXIMATED using the generic two-row USB-C 24-pin SMD land-pattern convention (cross-referenced against KiCad stock USB_C_Receptacle_JAE_DX07S024WJ1R350) and are NOT pixel-digitized off the HRO drawing -- verify against HRO's CAD/STEP file or physical measurement before finalizing fab layout. See task-14 J1 footprint report for full detail.")
	(tags "USB C Type-C Receptacle USB3 SuperSpeed HRO TYPE-C-31 24-pin full-featured")
